-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  mod_kinds.pcpp - Module compliance: the module kinds exe, dll, lib, unit and
  the module body

  module exe | dll | lib | unit <name>; (BNF.md sec 1). An exe emits an
  executable and must have a begin body; a dll (shared library), a lib (static
  library) and a unit end with end. alone. A unit emits nothing of its own: it
  is compiled into the build of every module that imports it, and it cannot be
  the main module. This exe imports the unit mod_kinds_unit.pcpp and prints
  what its routine returns. The dll and lib kinds are mod_kinds_dll.pcpp and
  mod_kinds_lib.pcpp, each checked by building it (their own headers).

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\mod_kinds.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\mod_kinds.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    the exe body runs
    mod_kinds_unit.Answer() = 42
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  Both targets print the same; the [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way; each reports exactly what the
  // ERROR / WARN / HINT comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    mod_kinds_err_kind.pcpp       no module kind after module
    mod_kinds_err_unitmain.pcpp   a unit handed to the compiler as the main module
    mod_kinds_err_body.pcpp       a begin body in a lib
    mod_kinds_err_nobody.pcpp     an exe without a begin body
    mod_kinds_err_afterend.pcpp   text after the module's end.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe mod_kinds;
import mod_kinds_unit;

begin
  println("the exe body runs");
  println("mod_kinds_unit.Answer() = {}", mod_kinds_unit.Answer());
end.
